course: dictionary
lesson: 7928
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them tell you which meaning the writer means. Reading is one of these words. «Reading and writing are the first things we learn at school.» Here reading means looking at written words and understanding them.
explain: «Vets often take a pet's temperature with a thermometer, because it gives an accurate reading.» Here a reading is a number shown on a measuring tool. The clue is thermometer. Ask yourself what would fit, then try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: «In Reading, Elsie's mum is a nurse and her dad is a teacher.» Here Reading, with a capital R, is the name of a town in England, said «RED-ing». The capital letter and the way it is used as a name are the clues.
fact: Reading means looking at written words and understanding them.
fact: A reading can be a piece of writing read aloud to people, as in church or at a wedding.
fact: A reading can be a number shown on a measuring tool, like a thermometer or a meter.
fact: A reading can also mean the way you understand something, an interpretation.
fact: Reading with a capital R is a town in England, said «RED-ing».
exercise: «Reading and writing are the first things we learn at school.» What does reading mean here? | A piece of writing read aloud in church | A town in England | *Looking at written words and understanding them | A number shown on a thermometer
exercise: «Vets often take a pet's temperature with a thermometer, because it gives an accurate reading.» What is a reading here? | A piece of writing read aloud to people | A book about animals | The name of a town | *A number shown on a measuring tool
exercise: «In Reading, Elsie's mum is a nurse.» What is Reading here? | A piece of writing read in church | A number on a meter | *A town in England | Looking at written words
test: «The first reading at the wedding was a poem about love.» What is a reading here? | *A piece of writing read aloud to people | Looking at words silently | A town in England | A number shown on a thermometer
test: «The science pupils wrote down each reading from the thermometer.» What is a reading here? | The name of a town | A way of understanding a poem | *A number shown on the thermometer | A piece of writing read aloud
exam: «Tom's reading of the poem was very different from Sam's.» What does reading mean here? | A number shown on a meter | *The way Tom understood the poem | A piece of writing read aloud in church | A town in England
